's free daily neuron budget without a single point of failure.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_track_vs_programme", "label": "Track vs Programme (two learning layers)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The track is kept to one language/practice stack at a time so students never see two languages mixed; the programme (year planning + competency framework) governs projects. Separating them lets switching tracks lose nothing and lets a programme's classes run different briefs while sharing the same concepts.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_programme_youcode_dwwm_a1", "label": "YouCode DWWM A1 2026/2027 programme", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_competency_framework", "label": "Competency framework (C1-C8 technical, CT1-CT9 transversal)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_points_scoring_system", "label": "Points, scoring and anti-farming rules (RULES)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Limited challenge types (multiple choice, complexity, predict the output, find the bug, regex) pay full points for 3 solves/day, half for the next 2, then 0, capped at 150/day, to discourage grinding low-effort challenge types while never limiting write code, SQL, HackerRank problems, or assigned/teacher-given work.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_vscode_tracking", "label": "VS Code activity tracking", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_wakatime_extension", "label": "WakaTime VS Code extension (repointed to ClassBot)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_assessclaude_flow", "label": "Claude-assisted assessment workflow (outside the app)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Lets a teacher use Claude directly (copy/paste JSON) to generate and grade assessments without giving the AI an API key; exports strip names, Discord ids, GitHub logins and emails so student identity never leaves the dashboard, while a per-student reference (P01, P02...) keeps results matchable on return.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_classbot_assessment_v1", "label": "classbot-assessment@1 JSON format", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_classbot_grading_export_v1", "label": "classbot-grading-export@1 JSON format", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_classbot_grading_result_v1", "label": "classbot-grading-result@1 JSON format", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_debrief_process", "label": "Debrief process (assessment, project/GitHub checks, one-to-one, competencies, oral questions, mise en situation, level, comment)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributo